.TH ACCT\-TX 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.3.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
acct\-tx \- account\-model payments for xlm, algo and atom. Encoded transactions are base64 (each chain's native form)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
 acct\-tx: account\-model payments for xlm, algo and atom. Encoded transactions are base64 (each chain's native form).
 Balance / sequence / rounds come from the host\-side `utxo\-fetch \-\-chain xlm|algo ADDR` (this tool has no network).
 acct\-tx build   \-\-chain xlm  \-\-from G.. \-\-to G.. (\-\-amount STROOPS | \-\-sweep) \-\-fee STROOPS \-\-seq N [\-\-memo\-id N|\-\-memo\-text T] [\-\-max\-time UNIX] [\-\-testnet]
 acct\-tx build   \-\-chain algo \-\-from A.. \-\-to A.. (\-\-amount MICROALGO | \-\-sweep) \-\-fee MICROALGO \-\-first\-round N [\-\-last\-round N] [\-\-note T]
 acct\-tx keys    \-\-chain atom < hex\-private\-key                    \-> {"address","pubkey"} (public only; build needs \-\-pubkey)
 acct\-tx build   \-\-chain atom \-\-from cosmos1.. \-\-pubkey HEX33 \-\-to cosmos1.. (\-\-amount UATOM | \-\-sweep \-\-balance UATOM) \-\-fee UATOM
 acct\-tx multisig\-build  \-\-chain atom \-\-threshold M \-\-pubkey HEX33 [\-\-pubkey ..] \-\-signer IDX [\-\-signer ..] \-\-to cosmos1.. (\-\-amount UATOM | \-\-sweep \-\-balance UATOM)
 acct\-tx multisig\-sign   \-\-chain atom \-\-tx FILE \-\-expect\-to cosmos1.. < hex\-private\-key   (one cosigner; shows the payment on /dev/tty, signs after the code \-> {index,sig})
 acct\-tx multisig\-combine \-\-chain atom \-\-tx FILE \-\-part FILE [\-\-part ..]   (assemble the quorum's parts into a MultiSignature TxRaw; refuses below threshold)
 acct\-tx multisig\-decode \-\-chain atom < combine\-JSON   (re\-verify every member signature and the bitarray against the SignDoc)
 acct\-tx keys    \-\-chain rune < hex\-private\-key                    \-> {"address" (thor1..),"pubkey"}
 acct\-tx build   \-\-chain rune \-\-from thor1.. \-\-pubkey HEX33 \-\-amount RUNE_1E8 \-\-memo "~:name:.."|"=:ASSET:DEST:LIM" \-\-sequence N \-\-account\-number N [\-\-gas 20000000] [\-\-chain\-id thorchain\-1]
 acct\-tx sign    \-\-chain rune \-\-tx FILE \-\-expect\-memo "~:name:.." < hex\-private\-key   (shows memo + amount on /dev/tty, signs after the code)
 acct\-tx build   \-\-chain ton  \-\-from UQ.. \-\-to EQ..|UQ.. (\-\-amount NANOTON | \-\-sweep) \-\-seqno N \-\-valid\-until UNIX [\-\-comment T]
 acct\-tx build   \-\-chain ada  \-\-from addr1.. \-\-to addr1.. \-\-utxo TXID#IX:LOVELACE [\-\-utxo ..] (\-\-amount LOVELACE | \-\-sweep) \-\-fee LOVELACE \-\-ttl SLOT
 acct\-tx build   \-\-chain dot  \-\-from 1.. \-\-to 1.. (\-\-amount PLANCK | \-\-sweep) \-\-nonce N \-\-block\-number N \-\-block\-hash HEX [\-\-period 64]
 acct\-tx decode  \-\-chain C [\-\-testnet] < unsigned\-or\-signed (JSON from build/sign, or bare base64)
 acct\-tx sign    \-\-chain C \-\-tx FILE \-\-expect\-to ADDR [\-\-testnet] < secret   (xlm: S... ; algo: 25 words or base64 seed||pub)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Balance / sequence / rounds come from the host\-side `utxo\-fetch \-\-chain xlm|algo ADDR` (this tool has no network).
acct\-tx build   \-\-chain xlm  \-\-from G.. \-\-to G.. (\-\-amount STROOPS | \-\-sweep) \-\-fee STROOPS \-\-seq N [\-\-memo\-id N|\-\-memo\-text T] [\-\-max\-time UNIX] [\-\-testnet]
acct\-tx build   \-\-chain algo \-\-from A.. \-\-to A.. (\-\-amount MICROALGO | \-\-sweep) \-\-fee MICROALGO \-\-first\-round N [\-\-last\-round N] [\-\-note T]
acct\-tx keys    \-\-chain atom [\-\-hrp cosmos|osmo|juno|stars|secret|terra|cro|inj|zeta|evmos] < hex\-private\-key \-> {"address","pubkey"} (public only; build needs \-\-pubkey)
.nf
.RS 2
  \-\-chain atom covers Cosmos SDK MsgSend (SIGN_MODE_DIRECT, secp256k1) on the chains with a Trust Wallet Core vector:
  the chain is detected from the \-\-from hrp (cosmos=Cosmos Hub, osmo=Osmosis, juno, stars=Stargaze, secret, terra=Terra 2, cro=Crypto.org, inj=Injective, zeta=ZetaChain, evmos; inj/zeta/evmos use ethsecp256k1 + keccak256),
  plus 20 more hrps (stride axelar cre kujira comdex neutron somm mars umee noble sei celestia core quasar persistence akash
  kava band agoric dydx) whose vectors were generated by running TWC adf80f8 (not independent; docs/CHAINS.md),
  which sets the base denom and default \-\-chain\-id. Any other hrp is refused (cosmos_hrp_without_vector), as are
  Canto (TWC signs it as plain Cosmos, not ethsecp256k1), CosmWasm, IBC and every non\-MsgSend message.
.RE
.fi
acct\-tx build   \-\-chain atom \-\-from cosmos1.. \-\-pubkey HEX33 \-\-to cosmos1.. (\-\-amount UATOM | \-\-sweep \-\-balance UATOM) \-\-fee UATOM
.nf
.RS 2
                \-\-gas N \-\-sequence N \-\-account\-number N [\-\-chain\-id cosmoshub\-4] [\-\-memo T]   (unsigned = SignDoc, SIGN_MODE_DIRECT)
.RE
.fi
acct\-tx build   \-\-chain ton  \-\-from UQ.. \-\-to EQ..|UQ.. (\-\-amount NANOTON | \-\-sweep) \-\-seqno N \-\-valid\-until UNIX [\-\-comment T]
.nf
.RS 2
                (wallet v4r2 external message, BOC base64; deployed wallets only: seqno >= 1; the bounce flag follows the \-\-to form)
.RE
.fi
acct\-tx build   \-\-chain ada  \-\-from addr1.. \-\-to addr1.. \-\-utxo TXID#IX:LOVELACE [\-\-utxo ..] (\-\-amount LOVELACE | \-\-sweep) \-\-fee LOVELACE \-\-ttl SLOT
.nf
.RS 2
                (ADA\-only legacy outputs, change back to \-\-from; hex CBOR like cardano\-cli; UTXOs carrying native assets must not be used)
.RE
.fi
acct\-tx build   \-\-chain dot  \-\-from 1.. \-\-to 1.. (\-\-amount PLANCK | \-\-sweep) \-\-nonce N \-\-block\-number N \-\-block\-hash HEX [\-\-period 64]
.nf
.RS 2
                [\-\-spec V \-\-tx\-version V] [\-\-tip PLANCK]   (Polkadot Asset Hub Balances; UNVERIFIED layout, see recipes/chain\-polkadot.md)
.RE
.fi
acct\-tx decode  \-\-chain C [\-\-testnet] < unsigned\-or\-signed (JSON from build/sign, or bare base64)
acct\-tx sign    \-\-chain C \-\-tx FILE \-\-expect\-to ADDR [\-\-testnet] < secret   (xlm: S... ; algo: 25 words or base64 seed||pub)
.nf
.RS 2
  (dot: 0x\-hex mini\-secret as printed by recover, or the 12/24\-word mnemonic; ada: 128\-hex extended payment key kL||kR as printed by recover; ton: 24 TON words or 64\-hex ed25519 seed; signed JSON carries "pubkey" so decode can verify; atom: hex private key; signed JSON carries "signed" = TxRaw plus the "unsigned" SignDoc so decode can verify)
  shows the decoded payment on /dev/tty and signs only after the typed code. Prints {"signed":B64,"txid"}.
.RE
.fi
\-\-sweep: xlm = AccountMerge (moves the whole balance incl. reserve, deletes the account; fails while trustlines/offers exist);
.nf
.RS 2
         algo = amount 0 + close\-to (sends everything and closes the account; fails while ASAs are opted in).
.RE
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
                 \-\-gas N \-\-sequence N \-\-account\-number N [\-\-chain\-id cosmoshub\-4] [\-\-memo T]   (unsigned = SignDoc, SIGN_MODE_DIRECT)
                 \-\-fee UATOM \-\-gas N \-\-sequence N \-\-account\-number N [\-\-chain\-id ..] [\-\-memo T]   (m\-of\-n LegacyAminoPubKey, SIGN_MODE_DIRECT; \-\-signer fixes the quorum)
                 (THORChain MsgDeposit of THOR.RUNE; the action is the memo; native fee deducted by the chain)
                 (wallet v4r2 external message, BOC base64; deployed wallets only: seqno >= 1; the bounce flag follows the \-\-to form)
                 (ADA\-only legacy outputs, change back to \-\-from; hex CBOR like cardano\-cli; UTXOs carrying native assets must not be used)
                 [\-\-spec V \-\-tx\-version V] [\-\-tip PLANCK]   (Polkadot Asset Hub Balances; UNVERIFIED layout, see recipes/chain\-polkadot.md)
   (dot: 0x\-hex mini\-secret as printed by recover, or the 12/24\-word mnemonic; ada: 128\-hex extended payment key kL||kR as printed by recover; ton: 24 TON words or 64\-hex ed25519 seed; signed JSON carries "pubkey" so decode can verify; atom: hex private key; signed JSON carries "signed" = TxRaw plus the "unsigned" SignDoc so decode can verify)
   shows the decoded payment on /dev/tty and signs only after the typed code. Prints {"signed":B64,"txid"}.
 \-\-sweep: xlm = AccountMerge (moves the whole balance incl. reserve, deletes the account; fails while trustlines/offers exist);
          algo = amount 0 + close\-to (sends everything and closes the account; fails while ASAs are opted in).
.fi
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
acct\-tx keys    \-\-chain atom [\-\-hrp cosmos|osmo|juno|stars|secret|terra|cro|inj|zeta|evmos] < hex\-private\-key \-> {"address","pubkey"} (public only; build needs \-\-pubkey)
.nf
.RS 2
  the chain is detected from the \-\-from hrp (cosmos=Cosmos Hub, osmo=Osmosis, juno, stars=Stargaze, secret, terra=Terra 2, cro=Crypto.org, inj=Injective, zeta=ZetaChain, evmos; inj/zeta/evmos use ethsecp256k1 + keccak256),
                (ADA\-only legacy outputs, change back to \-\-from; hex CBOR like cardano\-cli; UTXOs carrying native assets must not be used)
.RE
.fi
acct\-tx decode  \-\-chain C [\-\-testnet] < unsigned\-or\-signed (JSON from build/sign, or bare base64)
acct\-tx sign    \-\-chain C \-\-tx FILE \-\-expect\-to ADDR [\-\-testnet] < secret   (xlm: S... ; algo: 25 words or base64 seed||pub)
.nf
.RS 2
  (dot: 0x\-hex mini\-secret as printed by recover, or the 12/24\-word mnemonic; ada: 128\-hex extended payment key kL||kR as printed by recover; ton: 24 TON words or 64\-hex ed25519 seed; signed JSON carries "pubkey" so decode can verify; atom: hex private key; signed JSON carries "signed" = TxRaw plus the "unsigned" SignDoc so decode can verify)
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
0
last status ok
.TP
1
last status error
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ printf '%064x' 1 | acct\-tx keys \-\-chain atom
# exit 0, last status: ok
$ printf '%064x' 1 | acct\-tx keys \-\-chain atom \-\-hrp osmo
# exit 0, last status: ok
$ printf '%064x' 1 | acct\-tx keys \-\-chain atom \-\-hrp canto
# exit 1, last status: error
$ acct\-tx build \-\-chain xlm
# exit 1, last status: error
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It may open hostile wallet files and handle secrets: run it sealed and offline (./blocktools run; sealed\-run allows it).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
